WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.734
♪ (MELANCHOLY MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.803 line:0%
Was the wife you played
kind of an idealization

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:04.904 line:0%
of the American wife?

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:05.905 line:0%
There is no such woman.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.841 line:0%
-Most of them are wretched nags.
-I don't think so.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.909
Yes, I think we all have
our moments.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.245
<i> Laura Petrie broke down
 and cried.</i>

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.748
<i> She was nasty
 and short tempered.</i>

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.650
<i> And she was also sweet
 and soft.</i>

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.852
And she was many things.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.655
Oh, no. I think she was
sort of a strained idealization

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.258
of the American woman,
as she thinks she is,

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.428
but it had no connection
with reality.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.064
SPEAKER:<i> Mary Tyler Moore
 was America's sweetheart.</i>

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.167
<i> Hardly anybody knows comedy
 like she does.</i>

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.970
SPEAKER 2:
<i> She was just masterful,</i>

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.004
<i> but she was also
 incredibly inventive.</i>

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:40.573
It's just that I couldn't go
to a party

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.775
knowing my son was
on the verge of being sick.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:46.079
MARY TYLER MOORE:<i> Carl Reiner
 saw some spark of humor in me,</i>

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.213
<i> and he started writing
 for me to be funny.</i>

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.884
SPEAKER 3:<i> She was on the side
 of risk taking.</i>

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.688
SPEAKER 4:
<i>Her morphing into Mary Richards</i>

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.491
<i> was such a feminist statement.</i>

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.294
SPEAKER 5:
The Mary Tyler Moore Show
<i> hired the most women,</i>

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.563
<i> and it changed the language
 of television.</i>

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.266
<i> Women speak differently,
 and we have different ideas,</i>

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.867
<i> and we have different stories.</i>

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.837
May you have
the pleasure and joy

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:14.073
of working
with Mary Tyler Moore.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.574
(APPLAUSE)

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.110
SPEAKER 6:
You were kind of locked up.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.814
The image on the screen
never matched the real Mary.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:25.685
SPEAKER 7:<i> She was no stranger
 to adversity.</i>

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.152
MARY:<i> I had a miscarriage,</i>

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.554
<i>and when I was in the hospital,</i>

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.024
<i> they discovered
 that I had diabetes.</i>

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.927
SPEAKER 8:<i> When Richie died,
 that really changed her.</i>

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.429
SPEAKER 9:<i> Just because you have
 a smile on your face</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.999
<i> doesn't mean you're not ready
 to go to battle.</i>

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.867
I believe in tomorrow.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.737
<i> I believe that things
 that are painful</i>

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.307
will not be as painful
in some time.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.610
<i> It's not the end of the world
 if I'm not perfect.</i>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.445
SPEAKER 10:
<i> Mary spoke to all of us.</i>

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.480
<i> Women could have careers,</i>

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.182
<i> could stand
 on their own two feet.</i>

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.184
Mary, we love you very much.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.786
SPEAKER 11:
<i> Her seven Emmy awards,</i>

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.321
<i> her three Golden Globe awards,</i>

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.090
<i>and her Academy Award nomination</i>

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.626
<i> are only the beginning
 of the story.</i>

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.328
SPEAKER 12:<i> I think
 she was meant to spark fire</i>

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:10.996
<i> with a very delicate match.</i>

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.534
Women are, or should be,
human beings first,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.203
<i> women second,
 wives and mothers third.</i>

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.771
It should fall in that order.

